re": 29599, "tokens_after": 29599, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "edges_between_full", "args": {"u": 767, "v": 1635}, "result_digest": "0d56f4e6cb735019", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": false, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 767, \"v\": 1635, \"window\": [0, 100000]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 38403, "tokens_after": 38403, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_049448d4", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [767, 1635, 722, 302, 733], "window": [20674, 59073], "confidence": 0.6, "narrative": "767 (9 events) has no direct edge to 1635 (step_16). The only short route is 767->722->302->1635, but each of those hops occurred exactly once over the entire horizon (steps 11-13), so a strictly increasing chain with both inter-hop gaps <= 600 inside a 38k-wide window would be a coincidence rather than a mechanism. The intermediaries 302 and 733 are top-10 hubs (269 and 485 distinct partners; steps 14-15), meaning static reachability to 1635 is a popularity artifact shared by most nodes. No alternative bridge exists: the other out-neighbours of 767 (988, 1292, 1719) reach none of 1635's in-neighbours (steps 08-10). Volume, hub popularity and time-ignoring connectivity are therefore explained away, and no genuine time-respecting cascade is supported.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static connectivity (necessary but not sufficient):**\n- 767 is a low-activity node: 9 events, 9 distinct partners, out-neighbours {722, 988, 1292, 1719} (step_02, step_03).\n- 1635 has 11 events, in-neighbours {106, 133, 302, 733} (step_02, step_04).\n- There is **no direct** 767\u21921635 edge (step_16).\n- The only short static route is 767\u2192722\u2192302\u21921635 (steps 07, 11, 12, 13), plus longer hub-mediated variants through 733.\n\n**Confounder controls:**\n- The intermediary 302 (344 events, 269 partners) and 733 (674 events, 485 partners) are among the top-most-active nodes in the graph (step_14, step_15). Almost every node in this graph is statically \"connected\" to 1635 through these hubs \u2014 reachability here is a popularity artifact, not evidence of a cascade.\n- Each of the three candidate hops (767\u2192722, 722\u2192302, 302\u21921635) fired **exactly once** over the whole horizon (steps 11\u201313). A single-shot chain must, by chance, land in strictly increasing order with **both** gaps \u2264 600 inside a 38,399-unit window \u2014 a very small share of the possible orderings. With 767 contributing only 9 events total, there is no repeated activity that could give the chain multiple chances to align.\n- No alternate short path exists: 988, 1292, 1719 lead to {233, 996, 1439, 1894}, {108}, {183, 353, 546, 1511} (steps 08\u201310), none of which are in-neighbours of 1635.\n\n**Conclusion:** the connection survives only when time is ignored and only via mega-hub intermediaries; there is no evidence of a tight (\u2264600) time-respecting relay, and the single-firing structure makes one improbable.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_049448d4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [767, 1635, 722, 302, 733],\n  \"window\": [20674, 59073],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"767 (9 events) has no direct edge to 1635 (step_16). The only short route is 767->722->302->1635, but each of those hops occurred exactly once over the entire horizon (steps 11-13), so a strictly increasing chain with both inter-hop gaps <= 600 inside a 38k-wide window would be a coincidence rather than a mechanism. The intermediaries 302 and 733 are top-10 hubs (269 and 485 distinct partners; steps 14-15), meaning static reachability to 1635 is a popularity artifact shared by most nodes. No alternative bridge exists: the other out-neighbours of 767 (988, 1292, 1719) reach none of 1635's in-neighbours (steps 08-10). Volume, hub popularity and time-ignoring connectivity are therefore explained away, and no genuine time-respecting cascade is supported.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 47348, "total_output_tokens": 5431, "total_tokens": 52779, "total_latency_ms": 78032, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}